## Build and deploy by hand

The manifests name the service image `calm-service:dev`. Build it under that name inside the cluster's container
runtime, then apply the base to a namespace. Point `kubectl` at that same cluster first (`--kubeconfig` and
`--context`):

```sh
minikube -p calm-backstage image build -t calm-service:dev .
kubectl create namespace {{serviceName}}
kubectl apply -k deploy/k8s -n {{serviceName}}
kubectl -n {{serviceName}} rollout status deployment/{{appNode}}
kubectl -n {{serviceName}} exec deploy/{{gatewayNode}} -- wget -qO- http://127.0.0.1:{{gatewayContainerPort}}/connections
```

To use another image name or tag, add a kustomize overlay with `images: [{ name: calm-service, newName: ..., newTag: ... }]`.

